  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nRidging continues to dominate the weather pattern across South \nTexas, maintaining hot weather for the foreseeable future. 500mb \nheights will remain around 590-595 dam throughout the week with \nsubsidence suppress convection, thus keeping rain chances slim to \nnone. 850mb temperatures also firmly remain around 22-27C with clear \nto mostly clear sky cover during the daytime. The Coastal \nBend/Coastal Plains area should see highs in the 90s with Brush \nCountry seeing temperatures in the upper 90s to triple digits \n(upwards of 108). Even with the slightly \"cooler\" air temperatures \nnear the coast, humidity will still amplify heat stress with heat \nindex values across the whole region forecast to peak between 104-\n116.\n\nA Heat Advisory will be in effect for most of South Texas Tuesday \nafternoon, excluding the Barrier Islands. Heat risk is forecasted to \nremain Moderate (level 2/4) to Major (level 3/4) on Tuesday and in \nthe days following, thus additional Heat Advisories may be \nwarranted. Localized Extreme (level 4/4) heat risk could develop \nover portions of the Brush County later this week. Make sure to \npractice heat safety whenever possible. Drink plenty of water, wear \nloose fitting clothing and take breaks in the shade/indoors to cool \noff. \n\nHGX - 03",
